# appease — fail
#
# Gentling a hostile beast out of hostility, and missing.
#
# The failure does NOT produce an outcome block: the beast is an enemy standing in the same area, so
# a failed action in front of it is an opportunity attack and the game goes straight to Fighting
# (ProximityModel — effective-Visual threat + failure ⇒ fight). Asserting "FAILURE" here would be
# asserting the wrong thing; what this proves is that missing an appeasement has teeth.
#
# --spawn-beast is what makes this reachable: appease only applies to an ENEMY (or an annoying
# acquaintance), and a wilderness factory rolls a beast 10–40% of the time and then lets it roam.
# The spawned one is flagged an enemy by the same first-contact pass that flags a rolled one.
#
# This used to exist only as the first half of cli/tame/success.cli — a beast that still wants to
# kill you cannot be tamed, so taming is appease-then-tame. Split out so the verb has its own test.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Den" --period noon --observe-only wolf

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect wolf

strategy fail-dice
goal appease
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue

# Drain the outcome preview. The fight is queued as a pending outcome and only starts once that box
# is committed — without this the script sits in LocationInteraction waiting for a mode change that
# is itself waiting on a CONTINUE.
advance 12 180

# The fight, not an outcome banner. Reaching Fighting mode at all is the assertion: a failed
# appeasement in front of a hostile beast is an opportunity attack, so there is no outcome block to
# read — asserting "FAILURE" here would be asserting the wrong thing.
wait mode Fighting 60

# What makes this an appease test rather than an any-verb test.
expect-verb appease
# The failure assertion that means something: the verb's own consequence did NOT happen.
# Asserting the wound instead would be flaky — FailurePenalties samples one slot in five,
# so most failures injure nobody.
expect-no-outcome affinity_change
quit
